    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0447" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/901</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received December</hi>
                        5.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 359</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s unnumbered
                    instruction of June 23, 1919<anchor n="54" xml:id="d314-f1"/> regarding the
                    currency reform in Haiti, I have the honor to forward herewith copy of the
                    Haitian official Gazette <hi rendition="#italic">Le Moniteur</hi> of May 7,
                    1919, containing the Convention of April 12, 1919, between the Haitian
                    Government and the Banque Nationale de la République d’Haïti, regulating the
                    monetary reform in Haiti, together with the Law of Sanction,<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d314-f2"/> and copy of the same Gazette of November 8, 1919
                    containing an additional act dated October 24, 1919, to the above Convention,
                    and the Law of Sanction.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d314-f3"/> Translations of these
                        Laws,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d314-f4"/> the Convention and the additional act
                    are also enclosed.</p>
                <p>Regarding the Protocol it was forwarded to the Department in my No. 352 of
                    October 6, 1919.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d314-f5"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A.
                    Bailly-Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d314-a1.xml" xpointer="d314-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d314-a2.xml" xpointer="d314-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d314-a3.xml" xpointer="d314-a3"/>
            </div>
